// EXPECT: PASS
// Phase-7 fragment-gate soundness demo, the FAIL-CLOSED direction. This postcondition is TRUE — a
// nonnegative integer divided by 2 stays nonnegative — so with z3 present the check PASSES. But the
// obligation lowers to `bvsdiv`, whose bit-blast is NOT in the machine-checked fragment (division is
// deferred BY DESIGN). So under `ANUBIS_NATIVE_AUTHORITATIVE=1` with z3 REMOVED from PATH, the native
// lane DECLINES (fragment gate → defer) and, with no z3 to fall through to, the check FAILS CLOSED
// rather than certify a property on an unproven blast. That is the whole point of the gate: a z3-free
// native proof rests only on proven wiring. (Contrast int_contract_proves.anb, whose every op —
// bvadd, comparators, bitwise, sub/neg, ite, and now both shifts — is machine-checked.)
pub fn half_nonneg(x: int) -> int
    requires(x >= 0)
    ensures(result >= 0)
{
    return x / 2;
}

fn main() {
    print(0);
}
